      "essay": "Though deceptively simple, this scene conveys a meaningful message: in a newly built community park, several residents exercise joyfully near trees and fitness facilities, with one saying, \"The new small park near home is really nice,\" while the accompanying bar chart shows that, between 2020 and 2022, the number of parks in this city rose from about 406 to around 670, with 532 recorded in 2021. It serves as a compelling testament to the significance of improving city life. To begin with, experience suggests that improving city life finds direct expression in phenomena exemplified by the way people exercise in parks near their homes. This is hardly surprising, as people tend to favour behaviour they believe will have desirable consequences. However, we should recognise that social conditions fundamentally shape the choices available to individuals. From this perspective, a shared commitment to improving people's well-being can create the conditions for communities and nations to flourish in harmony, laying the groundwork for sustainable progress. An article published by Nankai University lends support to the view that improving city life plays an important role in fostering community prosperity. In conclusion, a rational consensus has emerged that both individuals and communities benefit immeasurably when improving city life guides action. Promoting this principle is therefore not merely advisable but essential for holistic development.",
      "zh": "尽管画面看似简单，却传递出深刻的寓意：在新建的社区公园里，几位居民在树木和健身设施旁愉快地锻炼，其中一人称赞：“家门口新建的小公园真不错。”旁边的条形图显示，2020—2022年，该市公园数量从约406座增至约670座，其中2021年为532座。它有力地证明了改善城市生活的重要性。首先，从经验上讲，改善城市生活直接体现在以人们在家附近的公园锻炼为代表的现象之中。这并不令人意外，因为人们倾向于选择自己认为会带来理想结果的行为。然而，我们应该认识到，社会条件从根本上塑造了个人能够作出的选择。基于这一认识，对保障和改善民生的共同坚持能够为社区和国家在和谐中蓬勃发展创造条件，为可持续进步奠定基础。南开大学刊载的一篇文章支持这样一种观点，即改善城市生活在促进社区繁荣方面发挥着重要作用。总之，人们已经形成一种基于理性认识的共识，即当改善城市生活这一目标指导行动时，个人与社区都能获得不可估量的益处。因此，倡导这一原则不仅可取，而且是全面发展的必要条件。"
