      "essay": "Though deceptively simple, this scene conveys a meaningful message: on a hillside overlooking their village, two elderly residents stand together, gazing at the vibrant dragon boat race below, with one remarking joyfully, \"How wonderful! The dragon boat race in our village is getting more and more lively!\" It serves as a compelling testament to the significance of cultural revitalization in rural areas. Cultural revitalization in rural areas has attracted attention, not least because of its far-reaching implications. At the individual level, it is reflected in the way people participate in cultural practices and preserve shared customs through dragon boat races, ultimately contributing to meaningful connections to history and community. National policies on cultural heritage preservation likewise focus on empowering individuals to appreciate traditional wisdom and integrate it with modern life. Beyond personal advancement, this principle can strengthen communities by enriching cultural life and fostering neighborhood ties, laying the groundwork for sustainable progress. This is in line with national strategies for rural cultural revitalization: as this principle takes root, cultural activities proliferate and younger generations embrace heritage with fresh enthusiasm. In conclusion, a rational consensus has emerged that both individuals and communities benefit immeasurably when cultural revitalization in rural areas guides action. Promoting this principle is therefore not merely advisable but essential for holistic development.",
